<p dir="auto" class="break-words">### Comparative Analysis: GWT, AIF, and RSVPâ€“CPG</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Theories of consciousness and cognition often rely on metaphors to convey their underlying mechanisms. Global Workspace Theory (GWT) and Active Inference (AIF) have become two of the most influential, each articulating cognition through the language of broadcasting or prediction. The RSVPâ€“CPG framework introduces a third voice, framing cognition as a rhythmic, non-equilibrium gait. A closer comparison clarifies both overlap and divergence.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span>**Mechanism.**</span>
GWT models the brain as a set of competing modules, where the â€œwinnerâ€ gains access to a central workspace from which its representation is broadcast widely. AIF instead frames the brain as a predictive engine, constantly minimizing variational free energy to unify perception and action; Baioumy et al. (2020/21) extend this to robotics, linking AIF directly to control architectures such as PID loops. RSVPâ€“CPG departs from both: cognition is neither a contest for global ignition nor a Bayesian equilibrium process. Instead, it unfolds as a sequence of chained cortical central pattern generators (CPGs), where each step smooths entropy constraints before yielding to the next.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span>**Metaphor.**</span>
The differences are clearest in metaphor. GWT leans on the <span>**stage/spotlight**</span> imagery, emphasizing selective ignition and access. AIF invokes the <span>**equilibrium machine**</span>, portraying cognition as a process of settling into minimal-surprise states. RSVPâ€“CPG, by contrast, offers a <span>**movement metaphor**</span>: cognition as gait, a continual rhythmic oscillation where progress comes not from balance but from perpetual imbalance â€” like walking, always falling forward into the next step.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span>**Memory.**</span>
Memory also takes on distinct forms across the frameworks. In GWT, memory is episodic, entering the workspace only when summoned or contextually relevant. In AIF, memory is statistical: priors embedded in generative models, shaping predictive inference hierarchically. RSVPâ€“CPG instead models memory as <span>**proxy loops**</span> entrained to the cortical gait â€” rhythmic side-cycles that bias future steps by maintaining resonant traces of past trajectories.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span>**Dynamics of Motion.**</span>
Here the contrasts sharpen. GWT dynamics hinge on discrete ignition: a representation either gains access or it does not. AIF dynamics are continuous, but always geared toward convergence â€” the brain as a system that seeks steady-state balance through prediction-error minimization. RSVPâ€“CPG resists both discreteness and equilibrium. Its dynamics are oscillatory, non-equilibrium, and perpetually forward-driven: cognition as a rhythmic descent along entropy gradients, never converging but always renewing.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span>**REM and Dreaming.**</span>
Each framework also offers a distinct account of paradoxical sleep. GWT interprets REM dreams as the workspace being filled internally, without external input. AIF sees REM as generative models free-running, testing predictions outside sensory correction. RSVPâ€“CPG, however, emphasizes rhythm: during REM, CPG chains desynchronize. The cortical cycle still runs, but its gait becomes uncoordinated. Out-of-phase loops drift, producing the surreal juxtapositions characteristic of dreams.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><span>**Synthesis.**</span>
Taken together, these three frameworks illuminate cognition at complementary levels. GWT provides a phenomenological account of conscious access. AIF formalizes cognitionâ€™s statistical grammar. RSVPâ€“CPG offers the oscillatory skeleton â€” the rhythmic substrate on which both broadcasting and prediction ride. By repositioning cognition as a gait rather than a stage or an equilibrium, RSVPâ€“CPG opens a new conceptual path: consciousness not as balance or spotlight, but as perpetual rhythmic motion.</p>
