<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Reading guide / intuition</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The skew terms (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Îº</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">R</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa,\mathbf{R}\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8805em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">Îº</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">Rv</span></span></span></span> in the sheet; <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>Î³</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\gamma K</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">iÎ³</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">K</span></span></span></span> on the graph) are the mathematical â€œlamphrodyneâ€ that turns pure entropy descent into a \emph{structured recurrence}: they break detailed balance and generate a preferred rotational order of network activationsâ€”exactly what the Oxford team reports.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The slow entropy field <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> modulates gain and frequency, creating behaviorally relevant variability and genetic sensitivity without destroying the clock.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The Hopf normal form \eqref{eq:hopf} guarantees a stable limit cycle near onset and yields closed-form predictions for period, amplitude, and phase ordering that can be mapped to MEG-derived HMM states and transition asymmetries.</p>
