<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">AI / RSVP-AI:
â€“ Cyclical Î¦â€“ğ’—â€“S attractors provide a built-in scheduler, forcing diverse computations to share bandwidth.
â€“ This prevents runaway overfitting or deadlock, paralleling how the cortex maintains flexible but ordered cognition.</p>
<hr>
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary" start="6">
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Mathematical Formalization</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The empirical results directly validate the RSVP limit-cycle PDEs I outlined earlier:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Hopf bifurcation yields oscillations with period 300â€“1,000 ms (matching MEG cycle rates).</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Skew-symmetric couplings (ğ›¾K in the graph model) create asymmetric transition probabilities, equivalent to TINDAâ€™s FO asymmetry matrices.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Entropy field S modulates cycle rate and strength, aligning with observed heritability and age-dependence.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">This positions Van Es et al. as an empirical anchor for RSVPâ€™s claim that cognition is fundamentally entropic cycling rather than linear computation.</p>
