<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Below is a self-contained Bayesian analysis plan that (i) treats the Oxford MEG result as data (HMM state time-courses summarized by TINDA FO-asymmetry matrices, cycle strength , and cycle rate ), (ii) links it to your RSVP limit-cycle model, and (iii) yields subject-level and group-level posteriors, including a fully Bayesian ACE (heritability) component for cycle rate. Statements about the dataset and findings are grounded in the uploaded paper.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Bayesian analysis for RSVP-framed cortical cycles</p>
