</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">1.1 Latent global cycle template</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Let  be the global circular positions of the  canonical networks on . This is the group-level cycle â€œclock faceâ€ that the paper reports as consistent across datasets.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Prior (exchangeable but softly ordered to break label symmetry):</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\theta_k \sim \mathrm{Uniform}(0,2\pi),\qquad
\text{with a soft prior that enforces cyclic spread (e.g., a repulsive prior).}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">A simple repulsive prior: penalize near-collisions by</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\log p(\theta) \propto -\lambda_{\text{rep}}\sum_{m&lt;n}\exp!\big(-\frac{d_\circ(\theta_m,\theta_n)^2}{2\tau_{\text{rep}}^2}\big),</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">1.2 Subject-specific phase warps</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Allow each subject a small global phase shift and dispersion:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\phi_s \sim \mathrm{vonMises}(0,\kappa_\phi),\quad
\theta^{(s)}<span>*k \sim \mathrm{vonMises}(\theta_k+\phi_s,\kappa*</span>\theta),</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">1.3 FO-asymmetry likelihood from circular order</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">TINDAâ€™s FO-asymmetry  encodes that  tends to follow or precede  over variable intervals. A minimal RSVP-consistent signal is a skew-sine of circular difference:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\mu^{(s)}_{mn} = \beta_0 + \gamma_s ,\sin!\big(\theta^{(s)}_m-\theta^{(s)}_n\big),</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Measurement model (Gaussian; you can use Student-t for robustness):</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">A^{(s)}<span>*{mn} \sim \mathcal{N}!\left(\mu^{(s)}*</span>{mn},,\sigma_A^2\right),\qquad m\neq n,\quad A^{(s)}_{mm}\text{ ignored.}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Notes:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The  form encodes direction: positive when  is after  moving clockwise.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">You can augment with even harmonics for richer motifs: .</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">1.4 Cycle strength as a derived (or modeled) quantity</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Cycle strength  increases when asymmetries align globally. Treat it two ways:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Derived posterior check: compute  deterministically from posterior  and  using the same scoring functional as the paper (maximize clockwise order, then compute ). Compare to observed  for posterior predictive checks (PPCs).</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Or add a measurement model:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">S_s \sim \mathcal{N}!\big(f_S(\theta^{(s)},\gamma_s),,\sigma_S^2\big),</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">1.5 Interval-duration stratification</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">To match the paperâ€™s binning result (cycles emerge strongly at longer ISIs), let  vary by bin :</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\gamma_{s,b} \sim \mathcal{N}^+( \gamma_{0} + u_s,\ \tau_\gamma^2),\qquad
A^{(s,b)}<span>*{mn} \sim \mathcal{N}!\big(\beta_0 + \gamma*</span>{s,b}\sin(\theta^{(s)}_m-\theta^{(s)}<span>*n),,\sigma*</span>{A,b}^2\big).</p>
