<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Cycle rate model and heritability (Bayesian ACE)</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The paper reports cycle rate  is heritable (ACE ), relates to age/sex, and is stable within person. Model  hierarchically with ACE:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Work on log-rate for positivity:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">y_s=\log r_s.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Fixed effects for covariates (age, sex, heart rate, session, etc.):</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">y_s = \alpha_r + X_s\beta_r + a_s + c_s + e_s.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">ACE random effects with kinship  (twins/sibs):</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\mathbf{a}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},,\sigma_A^2,\mathbf{K}),\quad
\mathbf{c}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},,\sigma_C^2,\mathbf{J}),\quad
\mathbf{e}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},,\sigma_E^2,\mathbf{I}),</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Optional RSVP link: allow  to depend on subject skew  and entropy-pacing parameter (below):</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">y_s \sim \mathcal{N}!\left(\alpha_r + X_s\beta_r + \eta_\gamma \log \gamma_s + a_s+c_s,,\sigma_E^2\right).</p>
<hr>
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary" start="3">
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">RSVP-consistent entropy pacing  (slow variable)</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Model a subject-level latent â€œpacingâ€ variable  that modulates both rate and skew:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\gamma_s \sim \mathrm{LogNormal}(\mu_\gamma + \xi_\gamma q_s,\ \tau_\gamma^2),\qquad
y_s \mid q_s \sim \mathcal{N}(\alpha_r + X_s\beta_r + \xi_r q_s + a_s+c_s,\ \sigma_E^2),\qquad
q_s \sim \mathcal{N}(0,1).</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Intuition: higher  (tighter entropy budget) â†’ stronger asymmetry and faster cycles, or vice versaâ€”learned from data.</p>
<hr>
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary" start="4">
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Task/replay behavioral coupling</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The paper shows cycle phase predicts memory replay likelihood and RTs around âˆ’500 ms. Include a trial-level regression:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Let  be HMM probability of state  at time  before the button press on trial . Define a phase score:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\psi_{st}=\sum_k w_k,\pi_{skt}(-500\text{ ms}),</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Reaction time model (log-RT for robustness):</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\log(\mathrm{RT}<span>*{st}) \sim \mathcal{N}!\left(\alpha*</span>{\text{rt}} + \beta_{\text{rt}},\psi_{st} + u_s + v_t,\ \sigma_{\text{rt}}^2\right),</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">For replay segments, use a logistic model:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\Pr(\text{replay}<span>*{su}=1) = \mathrm{logit}^{-1}!\left(\alpha*</span>{\text{rp}} + \sum_k \beta^{\text{rp}}<span>*k,\pi*</span>{sk}(u)\right),</p>
