<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The Core Idea</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Youâ€™re treating the brainâ€™s cycles of network activity (as found in the Oxford MEG study) as a kind of cognitive gait. Just like walking depends on linked central pattern generators (CPGs) in the spinal cord, thinking and remembering depend on cortical cycles that â€œstepâ€ through networks in a repeating order. In RSVP terms, these cycles are limit-cycles of the Î¦â€“ğ’—â€“S fields: scalar excitability, vector flow, and entropy pacing.</p>
