<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Cortical cycles: The cortex is modeled as a set of oscillators (one per large-scale network). They are connected in such a way that activity tends to move in a circle, with one network more likely to follow another than the reverse. This asymmetry creates a preferred order â€” the â€œgaitâ€ of cognition.</li>
