<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Coupling between layers: The cortical cycle and the CPG chains are linked. When a cortical network fires at a certain cycle phase, it nudges a matching CPG subchain. And the more synchronized the CPG chain is, the more it feeds back to strengthen the cortical cycle. This bi-directional link explains why movement, working memory, and cognitive control feel rhythmically tied together.</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Entropy pacing (S): A slow control variable modulates how tightly synchronized the system is.</li>
