<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Measures: Recovery trajectory of cycle phase/order; ignition markers (P3-like components); prediction-error signals.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Predictions.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">RSVPâ€“CPG: Rapid phase re-locking without wholesale reordering; gait persists.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">AIF: Strong PE signals followed by gradual convergence; weaker cyclic invariance.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">GWT: Episodic â€œignitionsâ€ restore access but lack continuous phase continuity.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Stats.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Time-resolved circular stability metrics; model comparison via Bayes factors across theory-specific GLMs.</p>
<hr>
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary" start="8">
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Robotics Bridge: AIF Controller vs RSVPâ€“CPG Scheduler</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Question. Do RSVP-style cycles improve robustness on top of AIF controllers (Baioumy et al.)?</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Design.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Platform: 7-DoF Franka Emika Panda (sim + real).</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Controllers: (a) AIF baseline (per arXiv:2005.05554v2), (b) AIF + RSVP scheduler (periodic gating of state-estimation/actuation), (c) PID.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Perturbations: Unmodelled dynamics, delays, external disturbances.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Predictions.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">AIF+RSVP reduces oscillations and recovery time via temporal gating, mirroring human cycle pacing; learned temporal parameter maps to Î¼/Î³ in RSVP.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Stats.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Mixed models on tracking error, energy, settling time; spectral analysis of control signals to verify imposed gait.</p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Cross-Cutting Metrics and Implementation Notes</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Cycle metrics: state order (Î¸), FO-asymmetry matrix, skew Î³, cycle strength, cycle rate.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Cross-layer synchrony: Î“Ï† from peripheral CPG proxies (EMG, respiration, HRV/RSA) and motor rhythms; PLV/coherence with cortical cycle.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Phase extraction: HMM/TINDA state time-courses â†’ circular phase; confirm robustness with Hilbert-phase of band-limited sources.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Statistics: Circularâ€“linear mixed models; von Mises regressions; Bayesian multilevel models; ACE for heritability; permutation controls; PPCs from your Bayesian generative model.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Confounds: Eye movements, arousal (pupil/HRV), respirationâ€”record and include as covariates; ensure no trivial stimulus-locking drives effects.</p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Preregistration Skeleton (per study)</p>
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Primary hypotheses: list RSVPâ€“CPG predictions (phase-specific effects, Î³ moderation, Î“Ï† mediation, REM desynchronization).</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Primary outcomes: cycle strength, rate, Î³; behavioral (RT/precision); REM bizarreness.</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Analysis plan: exact models, priors, handling of circular data, PPCs; correction for multiple comparisons via hierarchical shrinkage.</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Exclusion criteria: signal quality, excessive artifacts, task non-compliance.</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">Power: simulations using your Bayesian model to calibrate N for 95% posterior mass on effect sizes of interest.</li>
</ol>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">These protocols give you decisive, falsifiable tests: if behavior and memory hinge on phase-specific cortical cycles and if REM bizarreness tracks cross-chain desynchronization (not cycle loss), RSVPâ€“CPG explains phenomena that GWT and AIF only describe. If not, the Bayesian model will show precisely where the gait hypothesis fails â€” either in phase-specificity, cross-layer mediation, or heritability of coupling parameters.</p></div><section class="inline-media-container flex flex-col gap-1 clear-both"></section><section class="auth-notification flex flex-col gap-1"></section></div></div><div class="order-first sticky hidden @md/mainview:block top-11 h-0 opacity-0 group-focus-within:opacity-100 group-hover:opacity-100 -mr-[36px] @lg/mainview:-mr-12"><div class="min-h-7 py-4 flex flex-col gap-0.5"><button class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium leading-[normal] cursor-pointer focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed transition-colors duration-100 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 select-none text-fg-secondary hover:text-fg-primary hover:bg-button-ghost-hover disabled:hover:text-fg-secondary disabled:hover:bg-transparent [&amp;_svg]:hover:text-fg-primary h-10 w-10 rounded-full" type="button" aria-label="Editar" data-state="closed"><span style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="stroke-[2] size-4"><path d="M18.25 5.75C16.8693 4.36929 14.6307 4.36929 13.25 5.75L10.125 8.875L5.52404 13.476C4.86236 14.1376 4.45361 15.0104 4.36889 15.9423L4 20.0001L8.0578 19.6311C8.98967 19.5464 9.86234 19.1377 10.524 18.476L18.25 10.75C19.6307 9.36929 19.6307 7.13071 18.25 5.75V5.75Z" stroke="currentColor"></path><path d="M12.5 7.5L16.5 11.5" stroke="currentColor"></path></svg></span></button><button class="inl