="mord mtight"><span class="mrel mtight">â‰¤</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2452em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">where pruning inactive heads approximates hypothesis sparsification.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">% ============================================================
% PART V â€” Moderate Nativist Reconciliation
% ============================================================</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\part{Moderate Reconciliation with Nativist Constraints}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section{Where Bias Is, and Is Not}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The model accepts:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
\item Strong inductive biases for efficiency (hierarchical prediction, sparsity, locality, compositional reuse).
\item Innate constraints on perceptionâ€“action cycles, working memory bottlenecks, and entropy minimization pressure.
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">It rejects:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
\item Encoded symbolic grammars or algebraic syntax trees as primitive.
\item Language-specific innate operators.
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Thus, inductive bias exists, but exists at the level of predictive dynamics, not discrete symbolic formalisms.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">% ============================================================
