<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\section*{Future Work}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The framework developed here connects predictive geometry, sparse inference, attention dynamics, and embodied generative loops into a single account of linguistic and cognitive emergence. This synthesis opens multiple empirical, theoretical, and engineering directions. We group future work into five tightly-coupled research agendas.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\subsection*{1. Geometry of Predictive Manifolds}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">This paper formalizes semantic space as a Riemannian manifold endowed with the Fisher--Rao metric. Immediate research extensions include:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Computing \textbf{curvature spectra} (Ricci, sectional, and scalar curvature) of next-token manifolds in pretrained LLMs, and correlating them with reasoning complexity, surprisal profiles, and compositional reuse.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Characterizing \textbf{phase transitions} in manifold geometry across scale (model size, data quantity, training time) to determine whether reasoning ability corresponds to curvature flattening, dimensional collapse, or geodesic sparsification.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Evaluating whether human incremental sentence processing follows \textbf{shortest-path geodesics} in model manifolds, via eyetracking or self-paced reading datasets.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Testing whether logical contradiction, metaphor, and semantic anomaly occupy \textbf{negative-curvature regions}, predicting longer geodesics and higher predictive entropy.
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\subsection*{2. Mechanistic Tests of Auto-Autoregression}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Barenholtzâ€™s ``auto-autoregressive'' hypothesis predicts that learned predictors internalize their own continuation machinery. Future tests include:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Identifying whether transformers implement \textbf{internal hypothesis enumeration loops} during multi-step reasoning, detectable via recurrent attention motifs or cyclic state visitation.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Probing for \textbf{implicit world-simulators} by ablating components suspected to store reusable transition templates and measuring collapses in sample efficiency.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Testing whether successive transformer layers implement \textbf{iterative posterior sharpening} akin to belief propagation or Kalman-style smoothing.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Measuring representational \textbf{hysteresis} across long-horizon predictions to detect when a model becomes ``committed'' to a latent trajectory.
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\subsection*{3. Biological and Developmental Validation}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The cognitive interpretation of predictive geometry makes strong claims about human learning, none of which require language-specific priors. Experiments to evaluate this include:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Comparing child and model learning curves on \textbf{synthetic holographic-linguistic agnostic grammars} to test whether both rely on sparse template reuse rather than symbolic rule induction.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Measuring whether human learners show \textbf{sharp posterior collapse} onto a small set of continuations during comprehension, via information-theoretic analysis of eye movement entropy.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Testing whether infants exhibit \textbf{geodesic bias} in sequence learning tasksâ€”preferring low-curvature transitions over high-curvature, even when transition probability is controlled.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Using MEG/EEG decoding to evaluate whether neural next-word prediction signatures exhibit \textbf{natural gradient-like error propagation}.
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\subsection*{4. Scaling Laws and Efficiency Constraints}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">If language learning is sparse predictive inference, then efficiencyâ€”not data sizeâ€”determines asymptotic behavior. Future work will examine:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Whether scaling laws break when \textbf{posterior sparsity saturates}, predicting a regime where additional parameters add diminishing linguistic generalization.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Training small models with explicit \textbf{sparsity penalties on predictive hypothesis support}, testing whether this yields large-model generalization benchmarks with fewer parameters.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item Measuring \textbf{sample efficiency as a function of manifold intrinsic dimensionality} rather than parameter count.
\end{itemize}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\subsection*{5. Interpretability and Causal Interventions}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The geometric hypothesis yields unusually precise mechanistic probes:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{itemize}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item \textbf{Geodesic intervention}: steering hidden states along low-curvature directions and testing whether reasoning success rates improve.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item \textbf{Curvature surgery}: artificially flattening or sharpening local manifold curvature and evaluating effects on logical consistency, hallucination rate, and compositionality.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item \textbf{Posterior-editing interventions}: rewriting internal attention distributions to match the analytically-derived sparse posterior, and measuring alignment with Bayes-optimal predictions.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item \textbf{Counterfactual gradient routing}: forcing updates along or orthogonal to estimated Fisher directions to test whether learning performance is governed by natural-gradient alignment.
\end{itemize}</p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\subsection*{Grand Challenge Questions}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">These projects collectively aim to resolve a deeper scientific question:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\begin{center}
\textit{Is language intelligence the discovery of latent generative geometry under constraints of sparse continuation, rather than the acquisition of syntactic rules or symbolic primitives?}
\end{center}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">If correct, the consequences extend beyond linguistics and AI. Language would cease to be a special cognitive module or a cultural artifact encoded in the brain, and instead be understood as the \textbf{unavoidable equilibrium} of any sufficiently efficient system trained to recursively predict itself under limited bandwidth.</p></div><section class="inline-media-container flex flex-col gap-1 clear-both"></section><section class="auth-notification flex flex-col gap-1"></section></div></div><div class="order-first sticky hidden @md/mainview:block top-11 h-0 opacity-0 group-focus-within:opacity-100 group-hover:opacity-100 -mr-[36px] @lg/mainview:-mr-12"><div class="min-h-7 py-4 flex flex-col gap-0.5"><button class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium leading-[normal] cursor-pointer focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed transition-colors duration-100 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 select-none text-fg-secondary hover:text-fg-primary hover:bg-button-ghost-hover disabled:hover:text-fg-secondary disabled:hover:bg-transparent [&amp;_svg]:hover:text-fg-primary h-10 w-10 rounded-full" type="button" aria-label="Editar" data-state="closed"><span style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="stroke-[2] size-4"><path d="M18.25 5.75C16.8693 4.36929 14.6307 4.36929 13.25 5.75L10.125 8.875L5.52404 13.476C4.86236 14.1376 4.45361 15.0104 4.36889 15.9423L4 20.0001L8.0578 19.6311C8.98967 19.5464 9.86234 19.1377 10.524 18.476L18.25 10.75C19.6307 9.36929 19.6307 7.13071 18.25 5.75V5.75Z" stroke="currentColor"></path><path d="M12.5 7.5L16.5 11.5" stroke="currentColor"></path></svg></span></button><button class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium leading-[normal] cursor